          "title": "You'll want to know: حضارة",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حضارة — ḥaḍāra — \"a civilization\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "درسنا حضارة قديمة في المدرسة. darasnā ḥaḍāra qadīma fī al-madrasa. We studied an ancient civilization at school."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حضارة (ḥaḍāra) is built on the native Arabic root ḥ-ḍ-r (Lane), \"to be present\", the root of ḥaḍara, to attend, and of the taught ḥaḍḍara, to prepare. Lane gives ḥaḍāra as dwelling in towns and villages, the opposite of desert life."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
